# Keep every text file on LF so diffs never fight over line endings and
# shell scripts run under Git Bash on Windows. The line-endings CI check
# catches anything that slips past this.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary

# Append-only lists: every pull request adds a line at the end, so two of
# them always conflict there and never mean to. A union merge keeps both
# sides' lines. It applies to merges git does locally, which includes the
# merge queue's batch branch; GitHub's own conflict check ignores it, so a
# pull request can still show the conflict on the website while the queue
# merges it cleanly. Use it only for files where the order of new lines
# does not matter; the numbering check still catches a task added with a
# running number.
tasks.md merge=union
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
